<article class="env-lemma" id="05F4">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05F4">Lemma <span data-tag="05F4">32.4.10</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/086P" data-tag="086P">32.4.5</a>. Suppose we are given an $i$ and a locally constructible subset $E \subset S_ i$ such that $f_ i(S) \subset E$. Then $f_{i'i}(S_{i'}) \subset E$ for all sufficiently large $i'$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Writing $S_ i$ as a finite union of open affine subschemes reduces the question to the case that $S_ i$ is affine and $E$ is constructible, see Lemma <a href="/tag/01YX" data-tag="01YX">32.2.2</a> and Properties, Lemma <a href="/tag/054C" data-tag="054C">28.2.1</a>. In this case the complement $S_ i \setminus E$ is constructible too. Hence there exists an affine scheme $T$ and a morphism $T \to S_ i$ whose image is $S_ i \setminus E$, see Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00F8" data-tag="00F8">10.29.4</a>. By Lemma <a href="/tag/05F3" data-tag="05F3">32.4.9</a> we see that $T \times _{S_ i} S_{i'}$ is empty for all sufficiently large $i'$, and hence $f_{i'i}(S_{i'}) \subset E$ for all sufficiently large $i'$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>